From 7889eeea7af1ca14ae164df3fafc2ab9b402b582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:23:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(Core/Spells): don't clobber an escorting summon's
 movement (I-345)

Spell::SummonGuardian applied MoveFollow to MOTION_SLOT_ACTIVE after
Map::SummonCreature had already run InitSummon -> AI()->IsSummonedBy(),
so an AI that started an escort in that hook lost its movement slot to a
FollowMovementGenerator.

npc_escortAI::UpdateAI only launches its waypoint spline while
movespline->Finalized(), but zeroes m_uiWPWaitTimer either way, so when
the follow spline was still running the escort was stranded in
STATE_ESCORT_ESCORTING with no ESCORT_MOTION_TYPE generator - it trailed
the summoner forever and MovementInform could never revive it.

Visible as Khadgar's Servant (19685) refusing to walk the City of Light
(quest 10211) tour whenever the player was moving on quest accept.

Skip the follow when AI()->IsEscorted() reports an active escort, which
covers both npc_escortAI and SmartAI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp b/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
index 7d6b722aa..bb33820de 100644
--- a/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "Chat.h"
 #include "Common.h"
 #include "Creature.h"
+#include "CreatureAI.h"
 #include "DynamicObject.h"
 #include "Formulas.h"
 #include "GameObject.h"
@@ -6140,7 +6141,11 @@ void Spell::SummonGuardian(uint32 i, uint32 entry, SummonPropertiesEntry const*
         //    ((Minion*)summon)->SetFollowAngle(m_caster->GetAngle(summon));
 
         // xinef: move this here, some auras are added in initstatsforlevel!
-        if (!summon->IsInCombat() && !summon->IsTrigger())
+        // Map::SummonCreature() has already run InitSummon() -> AI()->IsSummonedBy(), so an AI that
+        // started an escort in that hook already owns MOTION_SLOT_ACTIVE. Overwriting it with a follow
+        // strands the escort: it keeps STATE_ESCORT_ESCORTING but never gets an ESCORT_MOTION_TYPE
+        // generator back, so it trails the summoner forever instead of walking its path.
+        if (!summon->IsInCombat() && !summon->IsTrigger() && !(summon->IsAIEnabled && summon->AI()->IsEscorted()))
         {
             //  summon->AI()->EnterEvadeMode();
             summon->GetMotionMaster()->Clear(false);
-- 
